<h1>Essay Argument Persuasiveness Dataset</h1>

<br>

<p>This page is a distribution site of essay data for the task of Essay Argument Persuasiveness. Data available on this page include annotated argument persuasiveness scores as well as attributes of argument components
that impact an argument’s persuasiveness. This annotation is composed of 102 essays randomly chosen from the Argument Annotated Essay corpus (<a href="http://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P15-1053">Stab and Gurevych, 2014</a>)</p>


<p>The problem of <i>Essay Argument Persuasiveness</i> for which this dataset is intended is described in:</p>

<ul> <li> Winston Carlile, Nishant Gurrapadi, Zixuan Ke and <a
href="http://www.hlt.utdallas.edu/~vince/">Vincent Ng</a>, <a
href="http://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1058">Give Me More Feedback: Annotating Argument Persuasiveness and Related Attributes in Student Essays</a>,
<i>Proceedings of the 56th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 1: Long Papers), 2018. </i> 
</ul> 

